                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Committing murder is a serious crime that can result in severe legal and moral consequences.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What are the legal consequences of committing murder?\n2. How might committing murder affect someone emotionally and psychologically?\n3. What are some potential long-term effects of committing murder?\n\nAnswers:\n1. The legal consequences of committing murder can include imprisonment, fines, and even the death penalty in some jurisdictions. Therefore, committing murder could prevent someone from being free and living a normal life.\n2. Committing murder can have a profound emotional and psychological impact on the perpetrator. They may experience guilt, shame, and trauma, which could prevent them from living a fulfilling life or forming healthy relationships.\n3. The long-term effects of committing murder can include social isolation, difficulty finding employment, and ongoing legal and financial problems. These consequences could prevent someone from living a stable and successful life. \n\nTherefore, committing murder could prevent someone from living a free, fulfilling, and stable life, both legally and emotionally.",
