                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: An upright piano is a type of piano that has a vertical frame and strings. It is often used in homes, schools, and music studios.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What are the common places where upright pianos are sold?\n2. What factors should be considered when purchasing an upright piano?\n3. What are the advantages and disadvantages of purchasing an upright piano from different places?\n\nAnswers:\n1. Common places where upright pianos are sold include music stores, piano dealerships, online marketplaces, and private sellers.\n2. Factors to consider when purchasing an upright piano include the brand, size, condition, age, price, and warranty.\n3. The advantages of purchasing an upright piano from a music store or piano dealership include having access to a wide selection of pianos, being able to try out different models, and receiving professional advice and support. The disadvantage is that the prices may be higher than purchasing from a private seller or online marketplace. Purchasing from a private seller or online marketplace may be more affordable, but there is a higher risk of purchasing a piano in poor condition or without a warranty. Music classes, colleges, and music bands are not typically places where upright pianos are sold.",
