                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "When someone is running, there are several things that could suddenly stop them. However, out of the given options, the most likely answers are B) falling down, D) exhaustion, and E) getting tired. \n\nIf someone trips or stumbles while running, they could suddenly stop due to falling down (option B). This could be caused by uneven terrain, obstacles in their path, or simply losing their balance.\n\nExhaustion (option D) could also suddenly stop someone when they are running. If they have been running for a long time or at a high intensity, their muscles may become fatigued and they may not be able to continue running.\n\nSimilarly, getting tired (option E) could also cause someone to suddenly stop running. This could be due to a lack of sleep, poor nutrition, or simply not being in good enough physical condition to sustain the activity.\n\nOption A, mushroom, is unlikely to suddenly stop someone when they are running as it is not typically found in their path. Option C, sweating, is a natural bodily response to exercise and would not necessarily cause someone to suddenly stop running. \n\nTherefore, the most likely answers to the question are B) falling down, D) exhaustion, and E) getting tired.",
