                        "cot": "How can a person suddenly stop while running?\nA) due to a mushroom\nB) by falling down\nC) because of sweating\nD) from exhaustion\nE) when getting tired\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n- A mushroom is unlikely to suddenly stop someone while running.\n- Falling down is a possible reason for someone to suddenly stop while running.\n- Sweating is a natural bodily function and does not directly cause someone to stop running.\n- Exhaustion can cause someone to suddenly stop while running.\n- Getting tired is a gradual process and not a sudden stop.\n\nTherefore, the correct answers are B) falling down and D) exhaustion.",
