                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Running is a physical activity that requires energy and endurance. It involves the use of muscles, joints, and the cardiovascular system. \n\nSub-questions:\n1. What happens to the body when someone runs?\n2. What factors can affect a person's ability to run?\n3. What are some common reasons why someone might suddenly stop running?\n\nAnswers:\n1. When someone runs, their heart rate and breathing increase to supply oxygen and nutrients to the muscles. The muscles contract and relax to move the body forward. The joints absorb impact and provide stability. \n2. Factors that can affect a person's ability to run include their fitness level, hydration status, nutrition, sleep, age, and any underlying medical conditions. \n3. Some common reasons why someone might suddenly stop running include exhaustion, muscle cramps, injury, dehydration, dizziness, or a sudden change in the environment (such as tripping or encountering an obstacle). Therefore, options D and B are the most likely answers. Options A, C, and E are not likely to suddenly stop someone when they are running.",
