                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Professor, can you explain to me what the primary purpose of cars is?\n\nProfessor: Sure, the primary purpose of cars is to move people.\n\nStudent: How do cars move people?\n\nProfessor: Cars move people by using an engine that converts fuel into energy, which then powers the wheels to move the car forward.\n\nStudent: What kind of fuel do cars use?\n\nProfessor: Cars can use different types of fuel, such as gasoline, diesel, or electricity, depending on the type of car.\n\nStudent: Why do cars need fuel to move?\n\nProfessor: Cars need fuel to move because the engine requires energy to power the wheels and move the car forward. Fuel provides that energy.\n\nStudent: So, the primary purpose of cars is to move people using an engine that converts fuel into energy?\n\nProfessor: Yes, that's correct. The primary purpose of cars is to transport people from one place to another using an engine that converts fuel into energy to power the wheels and move the car forward.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
