                        "cot": "How can a person who avoids leafy greens obtain minerals?\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n\n- Leafy greens are a good source of minerals.\n- If a person avoids leafy greens, they need to find other sources of minerals.\n- Option A, multivitamin, is a common way to supplement minerals in the diet.\n- Option B, farm, is not a specific enough answer. Farms can grow a variety of crops, some of which may be good sources of minerals, but not all.\n- Option C, Michigan, is not relevant to the question.\n- Option D, earth, is a general answer. Minerals can be obtained from the earth, but this does not specify how a person can consume them.\n- Option E, ore, is also a general answer. Ores contain minerals, but they need to be processed before they can be consumed.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A) multivitamin.",
                        "answers": [
