                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Traveling can be expensive and unexpected costs can arise during the trip. It is important to be prepared for these situations to avoid financial stress and potential disruptions to the trip.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What are some common unexpected costs that can arise during travel?\n2. How can one prepare for unexpected costs while traveling?\n3. What are some strategies for managing unexpected costs while traveling?\n\nAnswers:\n1. Common unexpected costs during travel can include medical emergencies, lost or stolen items, transportation delays or cancellations, and unexpected fees or taxes.\n2. To prepare for unexpected costs while traveling, it is important to have a budget and emergency fund in place before the trip. This can include setting aside extra money for unexpected expenses, purchasing travel insurance, and researching potential costs associated with the destination and activities planned.\n3. Strategies for managing unexpected costs while traveling can include prioritizing expenses and cutting back on non-essential spending, negotiating fees or prices when possible, and seeking assistance from travel insurance or emergency services if necessary. It is also important to stay calm and flexible in the face of unexpected costs, and to remember that unexpected expenses are a normal part of travel.",
                        "answers": [
