                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Coffee is a popular beverage that is consumed by people all over the world. It is made by brewing ground coffee beans with hot water. \n\nSub-questions:\n1. What are the common places where people consume coffee?\n2. What are the factors that influence where people make coffee?\n3. What are the advantages and disadvantages of making coffee in different places?\n\nAnswering sub-question 1: \n1. Common places where people consume coffee include coffee shops, offices, homes, restaurants, and cafes.\n\nAnswering sub-question 2:\n2. Factors that influence where people make coffee include convenience, availability of equipment, time, and personal preference.\n\nAnswering sub-question 3:\n3. Advantages of making coffee in different places include:\n- Coffee shops: access to a variety of coffee options, social atmosphere, and convenience\n- Offices: availability of equipment, free coffee, and convenience\n- Homes: cost-effective, customizable, and convenient\n- Restaurants and cafes: access to a variety of coffee options, social atmosphere, and convenience\n\nDisadvantages of making coffee in different places include:\n- Coffee shops: expensive, crowded, and noisy\n- Offices: limited coffee options, low-quality coffee, and lack of privacy\n- Homes: lack of access to specialty coffee, lack of social atmosphere, and lack of convenience when traveling\n- Restaurants and cafes: expensive, limited coffee options, and lack of privacy. \n\nAnswering the original question:\nBased on the sub-questions and answers, the most common place where people make coffee is in their kitchen (option E). This is because making coffee at home is cost-effective, customizable, and convenient. However, coffee shops and offices are also popular places where people make coffee.",
