                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The correct answer is D) family tree.\n\nTo understand why, we need to break down the question and the options provided. The question is asking what someone would have to add if they found out their brother was having a daughter. This means that the person's brother is going to be a father, and the person will become an aunt or uncle to their brother's child.\n\nThe options provided are:\n\nA) family picture book - This option doesn't make sense because a picture book is not a place to record family relationships.\n\nB) family reunion - This option doesn't make sense because a family reunion is an event, not a place to record family relationships.\n\nC) brother's house - This option doesn't make sense because a house is not a place to record family relationships.\n\nD) family tree - This option makes sense because a family tree is a visual representation of a family's relationships. If someone found out their brother was having a daughter, they would need to add a new limb to the family tree to represent the new niece.\n\nE) baby shower - This option doesn't make sense because a baby shower is an event, not a place to record family relationships.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D) family tree.",
