                        "cot": "Rephrased question: What would someone have to add to a certain item if they found out their brother was having a daughter?\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n\n- The question is asking about something that needs to be added because the person's brother is having a daughter.\n- The options are: family picture book, family reunion, brother's house, family tree, and baby shower.\n- A family picture book might include pictures of nieces and nephews, but it doesn't make sense to add a \"niece limb\" to it.\n- A family reunion is an event, not an item, so it doesn't make sense to add anything to it.\n- Adding a \"niece limb\" to the brother's house doesn't make sense either.\n- A family tree is a visual representation of family relationships, so adding a \"niece limb\" to it would make sense.\n- A baby shower is a celebration of the upcoming birth, so adding a \"niece limb\" to it doesn't make sense either.\n- Therefore, the answer is D) family tree.\n\nAnswer: D) family tree.",
