                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Communication involves the exchange of information, ideas, and thoughts between individuals. It can occur through various means such as verbal, nonverbal, and written communication.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is communication?\n2. What are the different means of communication?\n3. What did Sage like doing with his peers?\n4. What are the benefits of exchanging ideas with peers?\n5. What are the drawbacks of peer pressure?\n\nAnswers:\n1. Communication involves the exchange of information, ideas, and thoughts between individuals.\n2. The different means of communication include verbal, nonverbal, and written communication.\n3. Sage liked exchanging ideas with his peers.\n4. Exchanging ideas with peers can lead to new perspectives, insights, and knowledge.\n5. Peer pressure can lead to negative outcomes such as conformity and risky behavior.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the original question is A) exchanging ideas. Sage loved communicating and he liked exchanging ideas with his peers.",
