                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Fast food restaurants are a popular type of chain restaurant that serve quick, convenient meals typically consisting of burgers, fries, and other fried foods. \n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is the definition of a fast food restaurant?\n2. What countries have a high prevalence of fast food restaurants?\n3. How can we measure the number of fast food restaurants in a country?\n\nAnswering sub-question 1: \nA fast food restaurant is a type of chain restaurant that serves quick, convenient meals typically consisting of burgers, fries, and other fried foods. These restaurants often have a drive-thru or take-out option and are known for their affordability and convenience.\n\nAnswering sub-question 2:\nAccording to a 2021 study by Statista, the United States has the highest number of fast food restaurants in the world, with over 247,000 locations. Other countries with a high prevalence of fast food restaurants include China, Japan, and the United Kingdom.\n\nAnswering sub-question 3:\nThe number of fast food restaurants in a country can be measured by conducting a survey or using data from industry reports. This data can be used to calculate the number of fast food restaurants per capita or per square mile in a given country. \n\nAnswering the original question:\nBased on the information gathered from sub-question 2, the country with the most fast food restaurants is the United States.",
