                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Funerals are typically solemn occasions where people gather to mourn the loss of a loved one. It is important to show respect and empathy towards the grieving family and friends.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is the appropriate attitude to have at a funeral?\n2. Why is it important to show respect and empathy at a funeral?\n3. What are some behaviors that would be considered inappropriate at a funeral?\n\nAnswers:\n1. The appropriate attitude to have at a funeral is one that is serious and solemn. This means showing respect for the deceased and their loved ones, and acknowledging the gravity of the situation.\n2. It is important to show respect and empathy at a funeral because it is a time of mourning and grief for those who have lost someone close to them. Being insensitive or disrespectful can cause further pain and distress.\n3. Behaviors that would be considered inappropriate at a funeral include making jokes or inappropriate comments, being loud or disruptive, and not showing proper respect for the deceased and their loved ones.",
