                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: A cold is a common illness that usually does not result in death. However, in some cases, complications from a cold can lead to more serious illnesses such as pneumonia.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. Why was he afraid he would die from his cold?\n2. What are the common complications of a cold?\n3. What are the ways to prevent complications from a cold?\n4. What is the best course of action if someone is experiencing complications from a cold?\n\nAnswers:\n1. It is unclear why he was afraid he would die from his cold. It is possible that he had other underlying health conditions that made him more susceptible to complications from a cold.\n2. Common complications of a cold include sinus infections, ear infections, bronchitis, and pneumonia.\n3. Ways to prevent complications from a cold include getting plenty of rest, staying hydrated, taking over-the-counter medications to relieve symptoms, and avoiding smoking and exposure to secondhand smoke.\n4. The best course of action if someone is experiencing complications from a cold is to seek medical attention. This may include seeing a doctor, taking prescription medications, or being hospitalized if the illness is severe. It is important to seek help early to prevent the illness from becoming more serious. \n\nTherefore, the answer to the original question is E) seek help.",
