                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Being judged guilty can have a significant impact on a person's emotional state and self-esteem.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What are the possible emotions a person can feel when judged guilty?\n2. What factors can influence a person's emotional response to being judged guilty?\n3. How can a person cope with the emotions they feel when judged guilty?\n\nAnswers:\n1. The possible emotions a person can feel when judged guilty include controversy, responsibility, resentment, hurt feelings, and judge feelings.\n2. Factors that can influence a person's emotional response to being judged guilty include the severity of the accusation, the person's relationship with the accuser, the person's self-esteem, and the person's past experiences with being judged guilty.\n3. A person can cope with the emotions they feel when judged guilty by seeking support from loved ones, practicing self-care, seeking professional help if needed, and reframing their thoughts about the situation.",
