                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nFirst, it is important to note that hamburger meat can be contaminated with harmful bacteria such as E. coli or Salmonella. If the meat is not cooked properly, these bacteria can survive and cause food poisoning. Symptoms of food poisoning can range from mild stomach discomfort to severe dehydration and organ failure.\n\nIn addition, if the hamburger meat comes from a cow infected with mad cow disease, also known as bovine spongiform encephalopathy (BSE), the person who eats the meat can develop a fatal brain disorder called Creutzfeldt-Jakob disease (CJD).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C) mad cow disease.",
