                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Plan:\n1. Research the potential dangers of eating hamburger.\n2. Identify any specific risks or contaminants that could lead to death.\n3. Consider the symptoms and effects of each potential risk.\n4. Determine which option from the given choices aligns with the identified risks and symptoms.\n\nAnswer: \nBased on the plan, the correct answer is C) mad cow disease. Eating hamburger contaminated with the prion that causes mad cow disease can lead to a fatal brain disorder called variant Creutzfeldt-Jakob disease (vCJD). Symptoms include memory loss, personality changes, and difficulty with movement and coordination. While gas, getting full, feeling full, and death are all possible outcomes of eating hamburger, they are not specific to the risks associated with mad cow disease.",
