                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The correct answer is C) mad cow disease.\n\nMad cow disease, also known as bovine spongiform encephalopathy (BSE), is a fatal neurological disease that can be contracted by consuming meat from an infected cow. The disease is caused by abnormal proteins called prions, which can cause damage to the brain and nervous system.\n\nIf someone eats hamburger meat that is contaminated with the prions that cause mad cow disease, they can become infected and eventually die from the disease. Symptoms of mad cow disease include neurological problems, such as difficulty walking and speaking, and eventually lead to death.\n\nTherefore, option C) mad cow disease is the correct answer to the question of how someone can die from eating hamburger.",
                        "answers": [
