                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Additional facts: Hamburger is a popular food item made from ground beef. It is often cooked and served in various ways, such as in a burger patty or as a topping for pizza or pasta.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. Can hamburger cause food poisoning?\n2. What is mad cow disease and how can it be contracted?\n3. Can overeating hamburger lead to death?\n\nAnswers:\n1. Yes, hamburger can cause food poisoning if it is not cooked properly or if it is contaminated with harmful bacteria such as E. coli or Salmonella. These bacteria can cause symptoms such as nausea, vomiting, diarrhea, and in severe cases, kidney failure or death.\n2. Mad cow disease, also known as bovine spongiform encephalopathy (BSE), is a rare and fatal disease that affects the nervous system of cattle. It can be contracted by humans who consume contaminated beef products, such as hamburger, that contain the infectious agent responsible for the disease. Symptoms of mad cow disease in humans include dementia, muscle stiffness, and loss of coordination, and it can lead to death.\n3. Overeating hamburger alone is unlikely to lead to death, but consuming large amounts of any food can cause discomfort, bloating, and indigestion. In rare cases, overeating can lead to a condition called gastric rupture, which is a tear in the stomach lining that can be life-threatening. However, this is not specific to hamburger and can occur with any type of food.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "5b3bbf81-ed9f-47b2-bd9b-8b23bc2a6064",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-E",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "C) mad cow disease. Consuming hamburger contaminated with the infectious agent responsible for mad cow disease can lead to the contraction of the disease, which can be fatal. However, it is important to note that proper cooking and handling of hamburger can greatly reduce the risk of food poisoning and other health issues.",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
                        ],
