                    {
                        "id": "1263be50-f840-44e0-8d7f-b9f95d832350",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-17",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Professor, how can someone die from eating hamburger?\n\nProfessor: Well, there are a few ways that could happen. Which answer do you think is the most likely?\n\nStudent: I'm not sure. Can you explain each option?\n\nProfessor: Sure. Option A, gas, is unlikely to cause death from eating hamburger. Option B, getting full, is also unlikely unless the person has an underlying medical condition. Option D, death, is a bit too broad and doesn't really explain the cause. Option E, feeling full, is not a cause of death either. That leaves us with option C, mad cow disease.\n\nStudent: What is mad cow disease?\n\nProfessor: Mad cow disease is a neurological disorder that affects cows. When humans eat meat from infected cows, they can develop a similar disease called variant Creutzfeldt-Jakob disease (vCJD). This disease is fatal and there is no cure.\n\nStudent: How does the disease spread to humans?\n\nProfessor: The disease spreads to humans when they eat meat from infected cows. The disease is caused by a prion, which is a type of protein that can fold abnormally and cause other proteins to do the same. When humans eat infected meat, the prions can accumulate in their brain and cause damage over time.\n\nStudent: Is there any way to prevent getting mad cow disease?\n\nProfessor: Yes, there are a few ways to reduce the risk of getting mad cow disease. One is to avoid eating meat from cows that are known to be infected. Another is to cook meat thoroughly, as heat can destroy the prions. Additionally, some countries have implemented measures to prevent the spread of the disease, such as banning the use of certain animal parts in animal feed.\n\nStudent: Thank you for explaining that, professor. I understand now how someone can die from eating hamburger.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "34c24a80-5c10-456c-bd65-11e78b389699",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-E",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "C) mad cow disease.",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
                        ],
