                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Plants compete for resources such as sunlight, water, and nutrients in order to survive and reproduce. \n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is the neighbor of the flower? \n2. How do plants compete for sunlight? \n3. What are some strategies that plants use to compete for sunlight? \n\nAnswering sub-question 1: \nWe do not have enough information to determine the neighbor of the flower. \n\nAnswering sub-question 2: \nPlants compete for sunlight by growing taller or wider to reach more sunlight. \n\nAnswering sub-question 3: \nSome strategies that plants use to compete for sunlight include growing taller, growing wider, leaning towards the sun, and shedding lower leaves to reduce shading. \n\nAnswering the original question: \nBased on the information provided, we can infer that the neighbor of the flower likely grew taller or wider to also compete for sunlight. Therefore, the answer is D) cast shadow.",
