                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Death is the permanent cessation of all biological functions that sustain a living organism.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What are the biological functions that sustain a living organism?\n2. What happens to these functions when someone dies?\n3. Which of the given options are related to the biological functions that sustain a living organism?\n\nAnswers:\n1. The biological functions that sustain a living organism include breathing, circulation, digestion, excretion, and neurological activity.\n2. When someone dies, all of these biological functions permanently cease.\n3. Option A (moving) and option C (breathing) are related to the biological functions that sustain a living organism. Therefore, the answer is C) breathing.",
