                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The question is asking for the effects of drinking alcohol. \n\nStep 1: Drinking alcohol can lead to having fun, but that is not the only effect. \n\nStep 2: Drinking alcohol can also lead to intoxication, which is a state of being drunk or under the influence of alcohol. \n\nStep 3: Intoxication can lead to vomiting, which is the body's way of getting rid of the excess alcohol. \n\nStep 4: However, some people may continue to drink more alcohol even after vomiting, which can lead to further intoxication and potentially dangerous situations. \n\nStep 5: Another common effect of drinking alcohol is nausea, which is a feeling of sickness in the stomach. \n\nTherefore, the correct answers are B) intoxication, C) vomiting, D) drinking more alcohol, and E) nausea.",
