                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "How does drinking alcohol affect a person's body?\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n\n- Drinking alcohol is a behavior that can have various effects on a person's body.\n- Some people may drink alcohol to have fun, but that is not a direct effect of alcohol on the body.\n- Intoxication is a common effect of alcohol consumption, as it affects the brain and impairs judgment, coordination, and other functions.\n- Vomiting and nausea are also possible effects of alcohol consumption, especially if a person drinks too much or too quickly.\n- Drinking more alcohol is a behavior that can result from the initial effects of alcohol, such as feeling more relaxed or sociable.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B) intoxication, as it is a direct effect of drinking alcohol on the body. The other options are either behaviors or possible consequences of alcohol consumption, but not the primary effect.",
