                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Alcohol is a depressant that affects the central nervous system. It is absorbed into the bloodstream and can have various effects on the body and mind depending on the amount consumed.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. How does alcohol affect the body?\n2. What are the short-term effects of drinking alcohol?\n3. What are the long-term effects of drinking alcohol?\n4. What are the risks associated with excessive alcohol consumption?\n\nAnswers:\n1. Alcohol affects the body by slowing down brain function, reducing inhibitions, impairing judgment and coordination, and affecting the liver's ability to filter toxins from the blood.\n2. Short-term effects of drinking alcohol include feeling relaxed, talkative, and euphoric, but can also include slurred speech, impaired vision, and loss of balance.\n3. Long-term effects of drinking alcohol can include liver damage, high blood pressure, heart disease, and an increased risk of certain types of cancer.\n4. Risks associated with excessive alcohol consumption include addiction, alcohol poisoning, impaired driving, and an increased risk of accidents and injuries. It can also lead to relationship problems, financial difficulties, and mental health issues such as depression and anxiety.\n\nAnswer: Drinking alcohol can lead to intoxication, vomiting, nausea, and the desire to drink more alcohol. It can also have short-term and long-term effects on the body and mind, and can pose various risks to health and well-being.",
                        "answers": [
