                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Plan:\n1. Identify the potential outcomes of James competing.\n2. Evaluate each outcome to determine if it is a positive or negative result.\n3. Choose the outcome that aligns with James' goals and values.\n\nAnswer:\nBased on the options given, the potential outcomes of James competing are winning, performing better, making enemies, experiencing winners and losers, or losing. \n1. Winning would be a positive outcome as it would likely bring recognition and a sense of accomplishment. \n2. Performing better could also be positive as it would show improvement and growth. \n3. Making enemies would be a negative outcome as it could lead to conflict and negative relationships. \n4. Experiencing winners and losers is a neutral outcome as it is a natural part of competition. \n5. Losing would be a negative outcome as it could lead to disappointment and a sense of failure. \nBased on James' goals and values, he should choose the outcome that aligns with his priorities. If he values recognition and accomplishment, winning may be the best choice. If he values growth and improvement, performing better may be the best choice. If he values positive relationships, avoiding making enemies may be the best choice. Ultimately, the decision should be based on what is most important to James.",
                        "answers": [
