                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Professor, I'm a bit confused about the question. Can you explain it to me again?\n\nProfessor: Sure, James has decided to compete. If he competes, there are different outcomes that could happen. Which of the following is a possible outcome?\n\nStudent: Okay, I understand now. So, if James competes, he might win, perform better, have enemies, there will be winners and losers, or he could lose. Is that correct?\n\nProfessor: Yes, that's correct. Now, can you tell me which of these outcomes is not a possible one?\n\nStudent: Hmm, let me think. I think having enemies is not a possible outcome because it's not related to winning or losing.\n\nProfessor: Excellent! You're absolutely right. Having enemies is not a possible outcome of competing. Now, can you tell me which of the outcomes is the opposite of winning?\n\nStudent: The opposite of winning is losing.\n\nProfessor: Great job! You're doing really well. Now, can you tell me what the difference is between not competing and losing?\n\nStudent: Well, not competing means not participating at all, while losing means participating and not winning.\n\nProfessor: Exactly! You're really getting the hang of this. Keep up the good work!",
                        "answers": [
