                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: The question is asking for a place to store spare unused things that can be bought at a shop.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What types of shops sell storage containers?\n2. What are the different types of storage containers available?\n3. What are the pros and cons of each type of storage container?\n4. What size storage container do I need for my spare unused things?\n5. How much do storage containers cost?\n\nAnswers:\n1. Shops that sell home organization and storage products, such as The Container Store or Bed Bath & Beyond, sell storage containers.\n2. There are various types of storage containers available, including plastic bins, fabric bins, wire baskets, and wooden crates.\n3. Plastic bins are durable and waterproof, but can be bulky. Fabric bins are collapsible and lightweight, but not as sturdy. Wire baskets are stylish and breathable, but may not be suitable for small items. Wooden crates are sturdy and rustic, but may not be stackable.\n4. The size of the storage container needed depends on the size and quantity of the spare unused things. It is important to measure the items and choose a container that is slightly larger than necessary to allow for future storage.\n5. The cost of storage containers varies depending on the type, size, and brand. Prices can range from a few dollars to hundreds of dollars.",
