                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\"Two weeks after undergoing an emergency cardiac catherization with stenting for unstable angina pectoris, a 61-year-old man has decreased urinary output and malaise.\" This means he had a heart attack and had a stent placed.\n\"He has type 2 diabetes mellitus and osteoarthritis of the hips.\" This is a clue.\n\"Prior to admission, his medications were insulin and naproxen.\" This is another clue.\n\"He was also started on aspirin, clopidogrel, and metoprolol after the coronary intervention.\" This is another clue.\n\"His temperature is 38\u00b0C (100.4\u00b0F), pulse is 93/min, and blood pressure is 125/85 mm Hg.\"\n\"Examination shows mottled, reticulated purplish discoloration of the feet.\" This is another clue.\n\"Laboratory studies show:\nHemoglobin count 14 g/dL\nLeukocyte count 16,400/mm3\nSegmented neutrophils 56%\nEosinophils 11%\nLymphocytes 31%\nMonocytes 2%\nPlatelet count 260,000/mm3\nErythrocyte sedimentation rate 68 mm/h\nSerum\nUrea nitrogen 25 mg/dL\nCreatinine 4.2 mg/dL\nRenal biopsy shows intravascular spindle-shaped vacuoles.\"\nThe answer is eosinophilic granulomatosis with polyangiitis.",
