                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": " The patient has decreased urinary output and malaise. Laboratory studies show an elevated erythrocyte sedimentation rate (ESR) and elevated creatinine. A renal biopsy shows intravascular spindle-shaped vacuoles. The most likely cause of this patient's symptoms is cholesterol embolization. Cholesterol embolization is a complication of endovascular procedures, such as cardiac catherization, that can lead to renal infarction and ischemic nephropathy. The intravascular spindle-shaped vacuoles are characteristic of cholesterol embolization. The other options are not as likely causes of this patient's symptoms.",
