                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": " C. Xanthochromia on cerebrospinal fluid analysis would most likely be seen in this patient. Xanthochromia is a yellow discoloration of the cerebrospinal fluid (CSF) due to the presence of bilirubin, which is a breakdown product of hemoglobin. It is often seen in patients with meningitis, encephalitis, or other neurological conditions.",
