                    {
                        "id": "89d33b9c-7990-47e9-9b2d-f2e58aa36f0b",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-13",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "What is the class of immune cells that lyse abnormal cells without the need for opsonization, priming, or prior activation in a patient with monoclonal gammopathy?\n\nStep-by-step:\n\n1. The patient is a 67-year-old man with peripheral neuropathy who has monoclonal gammopathy detected by serum protein electrophoresis.\n2. The complete blood count, serum creatinine, and serum electrolyte concentrations are within the reference ranges.\n3. A bone marrow biopsy shows 6% monoclonal plasma cells.\n4. Further analysis shows that class I major histocompatibility molecules are downregulated in these monoclonal plasma cells.\n5. The question asks for the class of immune cells that lyse abnormal cells without the need for opsonization, priming, or prior activation.\n\nAnswer: D) Natural killer cells\n\nReasoning: Natural killer cells are a type of immune cell that can recognize and kill abnormal cells, including tumor cells and virus-infected cells, without the need for opsonization, priming, or prior activation. They do this by recognizing changes in the surface molecules of abnormal cells, such as the downregulation of class I major histocompatibility molecules seen in the monoclonal plasma cells in this patient. CD8+ T lymphocytes also have the ability to kill abnormal cells, but they require prior activation and priming. Bone marrow-derived macrophages and band neutrophils are not known for their ability to lyse abnormal cells. CD4+ T lymphocytes are involved in the adaptive immune response and do not have direct cytotoxic activity. Therefore, the best answer is D) Natural killer cells.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "784d2a20-d8df-45c8-8dc7-0dada4aac147",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-E",
