                        "cot": "\n\nD) Natural killer cells are the class of immune cells that lyse abnormal cells without the need for opsonization, priming, or prior activation. They play an important role in immune surveillance and defense against viral infections and cancer. In this case, the downregulation of class I major histocompatibility molecules in the monoclonal plasma cells may have allowed them to evade recognition and elimination by CD8+ T lymphocytes, which normally recognize and kill cells that display abnormal or foreign antigens on their surface. Therefore, natural killer cells may be the primary immune cells responsible for controlling the proliferation of these abnormal plasma cells.",
