                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nThe patient presents with progressive muscle weakness, difficulty with activities requiring shoulder and hip muscles, and difficulty swallowing solid foods. The neurologic examination shows moderate weakness in the arm abductors and hip flexors bilaterally, and laboratory studies show elevated creatine kinase and erythrocyte sedimentation rate. These findings suggest a myopathy, which is a disorder of the muscle tissue itself.\n\nOption A, intrafascicular infiltration on muscle biopsy, is a finding seen in some types of myopathies, but it is not specific enough to confirm a diagnosis.\n\nOption B, inflammation of synovial spaces on ultrasound, is a finding seen in joint disorders such as rheumatoid arthritis, but it is not relevant to the patient's symptoms.\n\nOption C, perifascicular and perivascular infiltration on muscle biopsy, is a finding seen in dermatomyositis, which is a type of myopathy that can cause skin rash in addition to muscle weakness. However, the patient does not have any skin rash, and this finding is not specific enough to confirm a diagnosis.\n\nOption D, positive anti-acetylcholine receptor antibodies, is a finding seen in myasthenia gravis, which is a neuromuscular disorder that causes muscle weakness due to impaired communication between nerves and muscles. However, the patient's symptoms and laboratory findings are not consistent with myasthenia gravis.\n\nOption E, dystrophin gene mutation on genetic analysis, is the correct answer. Duchenne's muscular dystrophy, which the patient's maternal uncle had, is caused by a mutation in the dystrophin gene, which leads to progressive muscle weakness and wasting. The patient's symptoms and family history are highly suggestive of this diagnosis, and genetic analysis can confirm it.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is E) Dystrophin gene mutation on genetic analysis.",
