                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The correct answer is D. Low dose dexamethasone suppression test.\n\nThe patient has Cushing's syndrome. The best next step in management is to perform a low dose dexamethasone suppression test. If the serum cortisol does not decrease, then the patient has bilateral adrenal hyperplasia. If the serum cortisol decreases, then the patient has an adrenal adenoma or carcinoma. In this case, the patient's serum cortisol did not decrease, indicating that she has bilateral adrenal hyperplasia.",
