                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "E) Theca lutein cysts, as they are the most likely cause of the ovarian findings described in the scenario. The presence of multiple thin-walled, septated cysts with clear content is consistent with the characteristics of theca lutein cysts, which are associated with high levels of hormones. The other options are less likely based on the given information.",
