                        "cot": " The patient has a thrombus in the left popliteal vein. The thrombus is located in a vein, not an artery. Therefore, the patient must have a condition that affects the blood clotting system. The answer is C) Deficiency in protein C.\nProtein C is a vitamin K-dependent glycoprotein that is synthesized in the liver. It is a major inhibitor of blood clotting, and it functions by inactivating two enzymes, Factor V and VIII, which are central to the blood clotting process. Protein C deficiency is an autosomal dominant disorder that is caused by a heterozygous mutation in the gene for protein C. The condition is characterized by recurrent thrombosis (formation of a blood clot within a blood vessel) and a high risk of fatal thrombosis.",
