                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Ribosomes are responsible for protein synthesis and use tRNA molecules to bring amino acids to the growing peptide chain. Each tRNA molecule is specific to a particular amino acid and has an anticodon that matches a codon on the mRNA sequence. Lysyl-tRNA synthetase is the enzyme responsible for charging tRNA molecules with lysine.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is the purpose of the experiment?\nThe purpose of the experiment is to investigate whether the ribosome can recognize a mischarged tRNA and still incorporate it into the growing peptide chain.\n\n2. What is the mischarged tRNA in the experiment?\nThe mischarged tRNA in the experiment is a Lys-tRNA charged with valine instead of lysine.\n\n3. What is the mRNA sequence in the experiment?\nThe mRNA sequence in the experiment contains only codons for lysine.\n\nAnswer:\nBased on the information provided, the most likely outcome is that the mischarged tRNA with valine will be incorporated in the codons that specify for lysine (option C). This is because the ribosome does not have proofreading mechanisms to check if the amino acid brought by the tRNA matches the codon on the mRNA sequence. As a result, the ribosome will incorporate the valine brought by the mischarged tRNA into the growing peptide chain. This can lead to a misfolded or non-functional protein. The other options are less likely because the ribosome does not have the ability to remove or degrade the mischarged tRNA or terminate protein translation due to an inappropriately inserted amino acid.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "658328bf-d259-496e-ade9-2384417bb2eb",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-E",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "C) The mischarged tRNA with valine will be incorporated in the codons that specify for lysine.",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
