                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nThe presence of a small pelvis, shallow intergluteal cleft, and club feet suggests a diagnosis of caudal regression syndrome (also known as sacral agenesis). This is a rare congenital disorder characterized by the incomplete development of the lower half of the body, including the sacrum and lumbar vertebrae.\n\nThe strongest predisposing factor for caudal regression syndrome is maternal diabetes. High blood sugar levels in the mother can lead to abnormal fetal development, including neural tube defects and limb abnormalities. Maternal diabetes is also associated with an increased risk of stillbirth.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D) Maternal diabetes.",
