                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The patient has a thyroid nodule that is suspicious for neoplasia based on cytological examination of a fine needle biopsy. Radioiodine therapy is planned after near-total thyroidectomy, indicating that the tumor is likely thyroid cancer. The question asks for the most likely initial metastatic site in this patient.\n\nThyroid cancer commonly metastasizes to regional lymph nodes, particularly the cervical lymph nodes. Therefore, the most likely initial metastatic site in this patient is C) Cervical lymph nodes. \n\nWhile other structures listed in the answer choices may be involved in metastasis from thyroid cancer, cervical lymph nodes are the most common site of initial metastasis. Tracheal invasion is a sign of advanced disease, and metastasis to the inferior thyroid arteries or thyrohyoid muscle is less common. Hilar lymph node involvement is more commonly seen in lung cancer.",
