                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Rephrased question: What LOD score would suggest a high probability of close linkage between the commonly found \u0394F508 mutation and a novel mutation in the CFTR gene in a particular population under study?\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n- LOD score is a statistical measure used to determine the likelihood of two loci being linked on a chromosome.\n- A LOD score of less than 1 suggests that the two loci are not likely to be linked.\n- A LOD score of 1 to 2 suggests some evidence of linkage, but not strong enough to conclude that the loci are linked.\n- A LOD score of 2 to 3 suggests moderate evidence of linkage.\n- A LOD score greater than 3 suggests strong evidence of linkage.\n- Therefore, the answer is D) LOD Score > 3, as this would suggest a high probability of close linkage between the two mutations. \n\nAnswer: D) LOD Score > 3",
