                    {
                        "id": "8e1a2044-e5f8-4fc8-abc3-7b3d9d9f0f7c",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-17",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Can you explain what a LOD score is?\n\nProfessor: Sure, a LOD score is a statistical measure used to determine the likelihood of two genetic loci being linked. It stands for \"logarithm of odds\" and is calculated based on the probability of observing a certain pattern of inheritance if the two loci are linked versus if they are not linked.\n\nStudent: Okay, so what does it mean if the LOD score is less than 1?\n\nProfessor: A LOD score less than 1 suggests that there is not enough evidence to support the idea that the two loci are linked. In other words, it is unlikely that the novel mutation and the \u0394F508 mutation are closely linked.\n\nStudent: And what about a LOD score less than 3?\n\nProfessor: A LOD score less than 3 suggests that there is some evidence to support the idea that the two loci are linked, but it is not strong enough to be considered significant. So, it is possible that the novel mutation and the \u0394F508 mutation are linked, but we cannot say for sure.\n\nStudent: What about a LOD score less than 2?\n\nProfessor: A LOD score less than 2 is similar to a LOD score less than 3. It suggests that there is some evidence to support the idea of linkage, but it is not strong enough to be considered significant.\n\nStudent: And what if the LOD score is greater than 3?\n\nProfessor: If the LOD score is greater than 3, it suggests that there is strong evidence to support the idea that the two loci are linked. So, in this case, it would be likely that the novel mutation and the \u0394F508 mutation are closely linked.\n\nStudent: And what does it mean if the LOD score is 0?\n\nProfessor: A LOD score of 0 means that there is no evidence to support the idea of linkage between the two loci. So, it is unlikely that the novel mutation and the \u0394F508 mutation are closely linked.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "4052f530-9fa1-4853-89bd-c244b0139d1d",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-E",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "D) LOD Score > 3, as it suggests strong evidence of linkage between the two loci.",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
                        ],
