formation provided, the most likely cause of the patient's symptoms is endometrial sloughing and uterine contractions mediated by prostaglandin. This is a common cause of menstrual cramps and pelvic pain, and the patient's symptoms are cyclical and related to her menstrual cycle. The fact that ibuprofen provides some relief also supports this diagnosis.",
