                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nE) Order an ACTH stimulation test\n\nThe patient's presentation is consistent with adrenal insufficiency, which can be confirmed with an ACTH stimulation test. The symptoms of fatigue, weakness, weight loss, and abdominal pain are all common in adrenal insufficiency. The bronze discoloration of the skin is also a classic finding in primary adrenal insufficiency, also known as Addison's disease. Treatment with hydrocortisone and fludrocortisone may be necessary depending on the results of the ACTH stimulation test. Androgen replacement therapy is not indicated in this case.",
