                        "cot": " The patient has a cord-like rash on her left calf that is red and painful to touch. She has had multiple such lesions previously and has had 3 past spontaneous abortions at < 10 weeks of gestational age. This suggests that the patient may have an autoimmune disorder. Autoimmune disorders are characterized by the presence of autoantibodies in the blood. The most likely autoantibody in this patient's blood would be anti-cardiolipin.",
