                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "we need to identify the patient's condition based on the given information. The patient presents with abdominal pain and constipation, with a history of right lower quadrant pain for 4 days. He has a fever, hypertension, and a history of smoking and poor diet. His colonoscopy from 1 year ago revealed multiple small polyps and colonic mucosal outpouchings. Based on these findings, the patient's condition is most strongly associated with:\n\nC) Ehlers-Danlos syndrome\n\nThis answer is incorrect. Ehlers-Danlos syndrome is a genetic disorder that affects the connective tissue, causing hypermobility of joints, skin that bruises easily, and other symptoms. It is not associated with the patient's symptoms or medical history.\n\nA) Alpha-1-antitrypsin deficiency\n\nThis answer is incorrect. Alpha-1-antitrypsin deficiency is a genetic disorder that can cause lung and liver disease. It is not associated with the patient's symptoms or medical history.\n\nB) Autosomal recessive polycystic kidney disorder\n\nThis answer is incorrect. Autosomal recessive polycystic kidney disorder is a genetic disorder that affects the kidneys and can cause liver and lung problems. It is not associated with the patient's symptoms or medical history.\n\nD) Goodpasture syndrome\n\nThis answer is incorrect. Goodpasture syndrome is an autoimmune disorder that affects the lungs and kidneys. It is not associated with the patient's symptoms or medical history.\n\nE) Menetrier disease\n\nThis answer is incorrect. Menetrier disease is a rare disorder that causes thickening of the stomach lining and can lead to stomach cancer. It is not associated with the patient's symptoms or medical history.\n\nThe correct answer is:\n\nDiverticulitis\n\nBased on the patient's symptoms, medical history, and colonoscopy results, the most likely diagnosis is diverticulitis. Diverticulitis is a condition where small pouches (diverticula) in the colon become inflamed or infected, causing abdominal pain, constipation, fever, and other symptoms. Risk factors for diverticulitis include a low-fiber diet, obesity, smoking, and a sedentary lifestyle. The patient's history of polyps and colonic mucosal outpouchings also suggest a predisposition to diverticulitis. Treatment for diverticulitis may include antibiotics, pain management, and dietary changes. In severe cases, surgery may be necessary.",
