                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "What is the next step in management for a 34-year-old patient with sinus tachycardia and an enlarged cardiac silhouette who cannot palpate radial pulse during inspiration after a motor vehicle accident?\n\nThe patient has signs of cardiac tamponade, which is a medical emergency. The next step in management should be to relieve the tamponade by performing a pericardiocentesis.\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n- The patient has sinus tachycardia and an enlarged cardiac silhouette, which are signs of cardiac dysfunction.\n- The inability to palpate the radial pulse during inspiration is a classic sign of cardiac tamponade, which is a medical emergency.\n- Cardiac tamponade occurs when fluid accumulates in the pericardial sac, compressing the heart and impairing its ability to function properly.\n- Pericardiocentesis is the definitive treatment for cardiac tamponade, as it involves removing the fluid from the pericardial sac to relieve the pressure on the heart.\n- IV Heparin, Chest CT scan, and Insert chest tube are not appropriate treatments for cardiac tamponade.\n- Pericardial window is a surgical procedure that may be considered in some cases of recurrent or chronic pericardial effusion, but it is not the first-line treatment for acute cardiac tamponade.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B) Pericardiocentesis.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "226a8334-ac38-471d-abb4-7e3a84ab4b0b",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-E",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "B) Pericardiocentesis.",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
                        ],
