ens is by creating pores in the cell membrane, which leads to cell lysis. This is specifically related to Neisseria infections, as Neisseria bacteria are susceptible to complement-mediated lysis. Therefore, option D is a possible answer.\n\nOption E) Induces the alternative complement pathway: The complement system can be activated through three different pathways: the classical pathway, the lectin pathway, and the alternative pathway. The alternative pathway is activated by certain bacterial and fungal cell wall components, and it leads to the",
