                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "What is the most appropriate initial step in treatment for a 16-year-old boy with fatigue, decreased academic performance, and abnormal laboratory values?\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n- The patient's symptoms and laboratory values suggest a possible diagnosis of iron deficiency anemia.\n- The low hemoglobin and MCV, high RDW, and nail and mouth changes are all consistent with iron deficiency anemia.\n- The patient's history and lack of other abnormalities on examination suggest that iron deficiency anemia is the most likely cause of his symptoms.\n- Therefore, the most appropriate initial step in treatment would be iron supplementation to correct the anemia.\n\nAnswer: D) Iron supplementation",
