                        "cot": "The patient's symptoms of eye dryness, foreign body sensation in the eyes, and oral mucosal ulceration and atrophy, along with the biopsy finding of lymphocytic infiltration of the minor salivary glands, are suggestive of Sj\u00f6gren's syndrome. \n\nSj\u00f6gren's syndrome is an autoimmune disorder characterized by dry eyes (keratoconjunctivitis sicca) and dry mouth (xerostomia) due to lymphocytic infiltration and destruction of the lacrimal and salivary glands. The presence of specific autoantibodies can help confirm the diagnosis.\n\nA) Anti-Sj\u00f6gren's syndrome type B (SS-B) antibody: This is also known as anti-La antibody. It is one of the two main autoantibodies associated with Sj\u00f6gren's syndrome (the other being anti-SS-A or anti-Ro antibody). The presence of anti-SS-B antibody supports the diagnosis of Sj\u00f6gren's syndrome.\n\nB) Anti-centromere antibody: This autoantibody is associated with limited cutaneous systemic sclerosis (scleroderma) and CREST syndrome (Calcinosis, Raynaud's phenomenon, Esophageal dysmotility, Sclerodactyly, and Telangiectasia). It is not typically seen in Sj\u00f6gren's syndrome.\n\nC) Anti-Jo-1 antibody: This autoantibody is associated with polymyositis and dermatomyositis, particularly in patients with interstitial lung disease. It is not typically seen in Sj\u00f6gren's syndrome.\n\nD) Anti-Scl-70 antibodies: This autoantibody is associated with diffuse cutaneous systemic sclerosis (scleroderma). It is not typically seen in Sj\u00f6gren's syndrome.\n\nE) Anti-double stranded (-ds)DNA: This autoantibody is specific for systemic lupus erythematosus (SLE). It is not typically seen in Sj\u00f6gren's syndrome.\n\nBased on the patient's clinical presentation and the associated autoantibodies, the most likely answer is:\n\nA) Anti-Sj\u00f6gren's syndrome type B (SS-B) antibody",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "68b10183-b80e-43e9-8b05-4a82f513195f",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-E",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "A) Anti-Sj\u00f6gren's syndrome type B (SS-B) antibody.",
                                "correct_answer": true
