.\n\nStudent: What are retrograde cytoskeletal motor proteins?\n\nProfessor: Retrograde cytoskeletal motor proteins are involved in the movement of materials within cells, from the cell periphery towards the center.\n\nStudent: What are anterograde cytoskeletal motor proteins?\n\nProfessor: Anterograde cytoskeletal motor proteins are involved in the movement of materials within cells, from the center towards the cell periphery. \n\nProfessor: Based on the patient's symptoms and medical history, the most likely answer is C) Transmembrane ion",
