                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nThe most likely cause is C) Rapidly progressive glomerulonephritis (RPGN). RPGN is characterized by a rapid decline in renal function, hematuria, proteinuria, and a hypercellular glomerulus with electron dense deposits along the glomerular basement membrane. Other causes of glomerulonephritis, such as PSGN, MPGN, MGN, and minimal change disease, can also present with similar symptoms, but the findings on renal biopsy are more suggestive of RPGN.",
