                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: The patient is experiencing tiredness and lethargy, has low hemoglobin levels, high serum creatinine levels, positive C3 nephritic factor, and proteinuria. The renal biopsy shows hypercellular glomerulus with electron dense deposits along the glomerular basement membrane.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is C3 nephritic factor?\n2. What is the significance of proteinuria?\n3. What is the significance of hypercellular glomerulus with electron dense deposits along the glomerular basement membrane?\n\nAnswering sub-questions:\n1. C3 nephritic factor is an autoantibody that stabilizes the alternative pathway C3 convertase, leading to persistent complement activation and glomerular injury.\n2. Proteinuria is the presence of excess protein in the urine, which can indicate kidney damage or disease.\n3. Hypercellular glomerulus with electron dense deposits along the glomerular basement membrane is a characteristic finding in membrano proliferative glomerulonephritis (MPGN), which is a type of glomerulonephritis that affects the kidney's filtering units.\n\nAnswer: B) Membrano proliferative glomerulonephritis (MPGN) is the most likely cause based on the patient's clinical presentation and renal biopsy findings. The positive C3 nephritic factor and hypercellular glomerulus with electron dense deposits along the glomerular basement membrane are characteristic of MPGN.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
