                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Can you explain what hemoglobin and serum creatinine levels are?\n\nProfessor: Hemoglobin is a protein in red blood cells that carries oxygen throughout the body. Serum creatinine is a waste product that is filtered out of the blood by the kidneys.\n\nStudent: What does it mean if the hemoglobin level is low and the serum creatinine level is high?\n\nProfessor: A low hemoglobin level can indicate anemia, which means there are not enough red blood cells to carry oxygen. A high serum creatinine level can indicate kidney dysfunction or damage.\n\nStudent: What is antinuclear antibodies (ANA) and why is it important that it is negative in this case?\n\nProfessor: ANA is an antibody that targets the nucleus of cells. A negative ANA test means that there is no evidence of autoimmune disease, which can cause kidney damage.\n\nStudent: What is C3 nephritic factor and why is it important that it is positive in this case?\n\nProfessor: C3 nephritic factor is an antibody that stabilizes the C3 convertase enzyme, which is involved in the complement system. A positive C3 nephritic factor test can indicate a type of glomerulonephritis called MPGN.\n\nStudent: What is proteinuria and why is it important that it is present in this case?\n\nProfessor: Proteinuria is the presence of excess protein in the urine. It can indicate kidney damage or dysfunction, as the kidneys should normally filter out protein.\n\nStudent: What is a hypercellular glomerulus with electron dense deposits along the glomerular basement membrane?\n\nProfessor: This is a characteristic finding on renal biopsy that can indicate a type of glomerulonephritis.\n\nStudent: So, what is the most likely cause of the patient's symptoms based on the information given?\n\nProfessor: Based on the information given, the most likely cause is MPGN, which is characterized by a positive C3 nephritic factor test, hypercellular glomeruli with electron dense deposits, and proteinuria.",
                        "answers": [
