                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The correct answer is D: Addition of sildenafil.\nThe patient likely has erectile dysfunction (ED), a common side effect of SSRIs. Sildenafil is a reasonable first-line treatment for ED.\nThe patient's symptoms of weak tumescence and low libido are likely due to his generalized anxiety disorder. The patient's dose of citalopram should not be lowered, as this could worsen his anxiety symptoms. Bupropion is not indicated for the treatment of ED. Switching to fluoxetine is also not indicated, as this would require a washout period of at least 2 weeks. Selegiline is indicated for the treatment of Parkinson disease, not ED.\nSildenafil is a reasonable first-line treatment for ED.",
