                        "cot": " \n\nThe first thing to consider is whether the patient's current medication is causing the sexual side effects. Citalopram is a common cause of sexual side effects, so the first step would be to lower the dose or switch to another medication.\n\nIf the patient's symptoms do not improve with a lower dose of citalopram, the next step would be to add bupropion. Bupropion is a norepinephrine-dopamine reuptake inhibitor (NDRI) that can increase libido and sexual function.\n\nIf the patient's symptoms do not improve with bupropion, the next step would be to switch to fluoxetine. Fluoxetine is a selective serotonin reuptake inhibitor (SSRI) that can also increase libido and sexual function.\n\nIf the patient's symptoms do not improve with fluoxetine, the next step would be to add sildenafil. Sildenafil is a phosphodiesterase type 5 inhibitor that can improve erectile function.\n\nIf the patient's symptoms do not improve with sildenafil, the next step would be to switch to selegiline. Selegiline is a monoamine oxidase inhibitor (MAOI) that can increase libido and sexual function.",
