ce and weight loss.\n\nProfessor: Based on the patient's symptoms and medical history, the most likely diagnosis is duodenal peptic ulcer (A). This is because the patient has a history of similar pain in the past, which occurs mostly after meals and often subsides several hours after eating. Additionally, the patient has lost a few pounds in the last couple of months, which could be a sign of a digestive issue. The physical abdominal exam is unremarkable, which suggests that there is no",
