                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "1. The patient is presenting with symptoms of difficulty breathing, especially at night, and a persistent cough. These symptoms suggest a possible issue with his heart or lungs.\n\n2. The patient has a history of a heart attack 5 years ago, which increases the likelihood that his current symptoms are related to a cardiac issue.\n\n3. The patient continues to consume alcohol despite being advised against it, which can contribute to the development of heart problems.\n\n4. The patient has already had an ECG and chest X-ray, which are initial diagnostic tests for heart and lung issues. The next step in management would be to further investigate the cause of his symptoms with a more specific test.\n\nConsidering all these factors, the most appropriate next step in this patient's management would be an echocardiogram (C). An echocardiogram is a non-invasive test that uses ultrasound to create images of the heart, allowing for the assessment of its structure and function. This test can help determine if the patient's symptoms are due to a cardiac issue, such as heart failure or valvular disease, which could be related to his history of a heart attack and alcohol consumption.",
