                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "What is the next step in the management of a 55-year-old man with severe cough, difficulty breathing, and a history of heart attack who presents to the emergency department and has an ECG and chest X-ray?\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n- The patient's symptoms suggest a respiratory and/or cardiovascular issue.\n- His history of heart attack and alcohol consumption are risk factors for cardiovascular disease.\n- The ECG and chest X-ray may provide clues to the underlying cause of his symptoms.\n- Angiography, CT, echocardiogram, stress test, and cardiac biopsy are all diagnostic tests that can help further evaluate the patient's condition.\n- Angiography is an invasive test that involves injecting contrast dye into the arteries to visualize blood flow and blockages. It may be indicated if the patient is suspected to have coronary artery disease or a pulmonary embolism, but it is not the next step in this patient's management.\n- CT can provide detailed images of the lungs and heart, but it may not be necessary at this point.\n- Echocardiogram is a non-invasive test that uses sound waves to create images of the heart. It can help evaluate the structure and function of the heart, and may be useful in this patient given his history of heart attack and symptoms of shortness of breath and cough.\n- Stress test involves monitoring the patient's heart rate and rhythm while they exercise or receive medication that simulates exercise. It can help evaluate the heart's response to stress and may be useful in this patient, but it is not the next step in his management.\n- Cardiac biopsy is an invasive test that involves taking a small sample of heart tissue for analysis. It may be indicated in certain cases of heart disease, but it is not the next step in this patient's management.\n- Therefore, the next step in this patient's management is likely to be an echocardiogram to evaluate his heart function and structure.\n\nAnswer: C) Echocardiogram",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "4e7d350d-7294-48b6-8795-d90f08473c19",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-E",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "C) Echocardiogram.",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
                        ],
