                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Can you explain what each of these options are and what they are used for?\n\nProfessor: Sure. Angiography is a test that uses dye and special x-rays to show the inside of your arteries. It's used to check for blockages or narrowing in the blood vessels. Computed Tomography (CT) is a type of imaging test that uses x-rays and computer technology to create detailed images of the body. It can be used to look at the lungs, heart, and blood vessels. Echocardiogram is a test that uses sound waves to create images of the heart. It can be used to check the heart's function and structure. Stress test is a test that measures the heart's response to physical activity. It can be used to check for heart disease. Cardiac biopsy is a procedure where a small piece of heart tissue is removed and examined under a microscope. It's used to diagnose certain heart conditions.\n\nStudent: Based on the patient's symptoms, which of these options would be the most appropriate next step?\n\nProfessor: Given the patient's symptoms, the most appropriate next step would be an echocardiogram. This test can help us evaluate the function and structure of the heart, which is important given the patient's history of a heart attack and his current symptoms of difficulty breathing and coughing at night. It can also help us determine if there is any fluid buildup around the heart or in the lungs, which could be contributing to his symptoms.",
