                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The answer is A) Defect in WASP gene.\nA defect in the WASP gene, which is responsible for the production of the WASP protein, is the most likely cause of this patient's symptoms. The WASP protein is involved in the activation of the NADPH oxidase complex, which is responsible for producing superoxide and other reactive oxygen species. The absence of WASP protein leads to a deficiency in NADPH oxidase activity, which can result in the symptoms seen in this patient.",
                        "answers": [
