                                "answer": " B) Gonadectomy. This is the most appropriate treatment for this patient's condition, as it is likely that she has a condition known as congenital adrenal hyperplasia (CAH). CAH is a genetic disorder that affects the adrenal glands and can cause a lack of menstrual periods. Gonadectomy is the surgical removal of the gonads, which in this case would be the ovaries. This would be the most effective treatment for this patient's condition.",
