                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nB) Gonadectomy\n\nThis patient's presentation is consistent with Mayer-Rokitansky-K\u00fcster-Hauser (MRKH) syndrome, which is characterized by the absence of the uterus and upper two-thirds of the vagina. Gonadectomy (removal of the ovaries) is the most appropriate treatment for this condition to prevent the development of ovarian tumors and to eliminate the source of estrogen production. Vaginal dilatory therapy may be used after surgery to create a functional vagina. Spironolactone and prednisolone therapy are not indicated for this condition. Testosterone therapy may be used in some cases of female hypogonadism, but it is not appropriate for MRKH syndrome.",
