                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Can you explain what \"transilluminates\" means?\n\nProfessor: Transillumination is a medical term used to describe the passage of light through a body structure. In this case, it means that when a light is shone on the scrotal mass, the light passes through it, indicating that it is a cystic structure filled with fluid.\n\nStudent: What does it mean when you say \"it is possible to palpate normal tissue above the mass\"?\n\nProfessor: This means that there is a layer of normal tissue between the mass and the skin of the scrotum. This is a good sign because it suggests that the mass is not attached to the testicle or any other important structures in the scrotum.\n\nStudent: What is the processus vaginalis?\n\nProfessor: The processus vaginalis is a structure that is present in the developing fetus. It is a pouch of peritoneum that extends into the scrotum and eventually obliterates (closes off) during fetal development. If it fails to obliterate, it can lead to the development of a hydrocele, which is a collection of fluid in the scrotum.\n\nStudent: What is the pampiniform plexus?\n\nProfessor: The pampiniform plexus is a network of veins that surrounds the testicular artery in the spermatic cord. It helps to regulate the temperature of the testicles by dissipating heat. Dilation and tortuosity of these veins can lead to the development of a varicocele, which is a swelling of the veins in the scrotum.\n\nStudent: Based on the information given, what is the most likely cause of the mass?\n\nProfessor: Based on the information given, the most likely cause of the mass is A) Imbalance of fluid secretion and resorption by tunica vaginalis, which is also known as a hydrocele. The fact that the mass is cystic, nontender, and transilluminates, and that there is normal tissue palpable above it, all point to this diagnosis. The other options are less likely based on the information given.",
                        "answers": [
