                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "A) Pulmonary embolism. Raloxifene is a selective estrogen receptor modulator (SERM) that is used to prevent and treat osteoporosis in postmenopausal women. However, it has been associated with an increased risk of venous thromboembolism, including pulmonary embolism. Therefore, patients taking raloxifene should be monitored for signs and symptoms of thromboembolic events. Cellulitis, breast cancer, mandibular osteonecrosis, and hypercholesterolemia are not known side effects of raloxifene.",
