                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Can you explain what the glucose concentration and potassium concentration mean?\n\nProfessor: Glucose concentration refers to the amount of glucose in the blood. In this case, the boy's glucose concentration was very low, which can cause symptoms like loss of consciousness. Potassium concentration refers to the amount of potassium in the blood. In this case, the boy's potassium concentration was also low, which can be caused by low glucose levels.\n\nStudent: What does it mean that a dextrose infusion was administered?\n\nProfessor: A dextrose infusion is a way to give the body glucose directly through an IV. It helps to raise the glucose concentration in the blood quickly.\n\nStudent: What is insulin concentration and C-peptide concentration?\n\nProfessor: Insulin is a hormone that helps the body use glucose for energy. C-peptide is a byproduct of insulin production. In this case, the boy's insulin concentration was very high, which is not typical for someone with low glucose levels. His C-peptide concentration was also low, which suggests that his body was not producing enough insulin.\n\nStudent: What is malingering?\n\nProfessor: Malingering refers to pretending to have symptoms or illness for some kind of gain, like attention or financial compensation.\n\nStudent: What is a glucagonoma?\n\nProfessor: A glucagonoma is a rare tumor that produces too much glucagon, a hormone that raises glucose levels in the blood.\n\nStudent: What is primary adrenal insufficiency?\n\nProfessor: Primary adrenal insufficiency, also known as Addison's disease, is a condition where the adrenal glands do not produce enough hormones, including cortisol and aldosterone.\n\nStudent: What is conversion disorder?\n\nProfessor: Conversion disorder is a condition where a person experiences physical symptoms that cannot be explained by a medical condition. It is thought to be caused by psychological factors.\n\nStudent: What is factitious disorder imposed on another?\n\nProfessor: Factitious disorder imposed on another, also known as Munchausen syndrome by proxy, is a condition where a caregiver intentionally causes or fabricates illness in someone else, often a child, in order to gain attention or sympathy.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "7180eadc-053a-4c21-a838-8212e18b94ed",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-E",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "B) Glucagonoma, as the high insulin concentration and low C-peptide concentration suggest that the boy's body was producing too much glucagon, which could be caused by a glucagonoma tumor.",
                                "correct_answer": false
                            }
                        ],
