                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Can you explain what G2P2L2 means?\n\nProfessor: Sure, G stands for gravida, which means the total number of pregnancies a woman has had. P stands for para, which means the number of live births a woman has had. L stands for living children. So, G2P2L2 means that the patient has been pregnant twice, given birth to two live children, and both children are currently living.\n\nStudent: What does it mean when the patient's previous menstrual cycles were regular?\n\nProfessor: Regular menstrual cycles mean that the patient's periods occurred at consistent intervals, usually every 28-35 days.\n\nStudent: What is the withdrawal method of contraception?\n\nProfessor: The withdrawal method, also known as the pull-out method, is a form of contraception where the male partner withdraws his penis from the vagina before ejaculation to prevent sperm from entering the woman's body.\n\nStudent: What is a urine pregnancy test?\n\nProfessor: A urine pregnancy test is a test that detects the presence of the hormone human chorionic gonadotropin (hCG) in a woman's urine. This hormone is produced by the placenta after a fertilized egg implants in the uterus, indicating that a woman is pregnant.\n\nStudent: What is an elective abortion?\n\nProfessor: An elective abortion is a procedure to terminate a pregnancy that is not medically necessary. It is a choice made by the patient for personal or social reasons.\n\nStudent: Can you explain the different procedures for elective termination of pregnancy?\n\nProfessor: Sure. Dilatation and evacuation (D&E) involves dilating the cervix and removing the contents of the uterus using suction and instruments. Oxytocin-induced labor involves using the hormone oxytocin to induce contractions and deliver the fetus vaginally. Manual uterine aspiration involves using a syringe and cannula to remove the contents of the uterus. Dilatation and curettage (D&C) after vacuum evacuation involves dilating the cervix and using a vacuum to remove the contents of the uterus. Oral mifepristone + misoprostol involves taking two medications to induce a miscarriage. In this case, the most appropriate procedure for elective termination of pregnancy would be E) Oral mifepristone + misoprostol.",
