                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Can you explain what hypertension and hyperlipidemia are?\n\nProfessor: Hypertension is high blood pressure, which can lead to damage to the blood vessels and organs over time. Hyperlipidemia is high levels of lipids (fats) in the blood, which can also contribute to cardiovascular disease.\n\nStudent: What do enalapril, furosemide, and simvastatin do?\n\nProfessor: Enalapril is an ACE inhibitor that helps lower blood pressure. Furosemide is a diuretic that helps remove excess fluid from the body, which can also help lower blood pressure. Simvastatin is a statin medication that helps lower cholesterol levels in the blood.\n\nStudent: What does it mean that the patient has epigastric tenderness and guarding?\n\nProfessor: Epigastric tenderness means that the patient experiences pain when the upper abdomen is touched or pressed. Guarding is a reflexive tensing of the abdominal muscles in response to pain or discomfort.\n\nStudent: What does it mean that the patient's hematocrit is 48%?\n\nProfessor: Hematocrit is a measure of the percentage of red blood cells in the blood. A hematocrit of 48% means that almost half of the patient's blood volume is made up of red blood cells.\n\nStudent: What does it mean that the patient's ECG shows sinus tachycardia?\n\nProfessor: Sinus tachycardia is a type of fast heart rate that originates from the normal electrical impulses in the heart. It can be a normal response to exercise or stress, but can also be a sign of an underlying medical condition. In this case, it may be related to the patient's abdominal pain and other symptoms. \n\nProfessor: Based on the information provided, the most likely underlying cause of this patient's vital sign abnormalities is capillary leakage. This can occur in conditions such as pancreatitis, which can cause inflammation and damage to the blood vessels in the pancreas and surrounding tissues. The leakage of fluid from the blood vessels can lead to decreased blood volume and low blood pressure, as well as other symptoms such as abdominal pain and nausea.",
