                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Can you explain what jaundice is?\n\nProfessor: Jaundice is a yellowing of the skin and whites of the eyes due to an excess of bilirubin in the blood.\n\nStudent: What is bilirubin?\n\nProfessor: Bilirubin is a waste product that is produced when red blood cells break down. It is normally processed by the liver and excreted in the bile.\n\nStudent: What does it mean when the liver edge is palpable?\n\nProfessor: When the liver edge is palpable, it means that the liver is enlarged and can be felt below the right costal margin.\n\nStudent: What is the significance of an increased alkaline phosphatase level?\n\nProfessor: An increased alkaline phosphatase level can indicate liver or bone disease. In this case, it is likely due to liver disease.\n\nStudent: Can you explain what CA 19-9 is?\n\nProfessor: CA 19-9 is a tumor marker that can be elevated in certain types of cancer, such as pancreatic cancer. It is not likely to be elevated in this patient.\n\nStudent: What are Kayser-Fleischer rings?\n\nProfessor: Kayser-Fleischer rings are a sign of Wilson's disease, which is a genetic disorder that causes copper to accumulate in the liver and brain. They are not likely to be present in this patient. \n\nBased on the patient's symptoms and laboratory results, the most likely additional finding in this patient is B) Cutaneous xanthomas, which are yellowish deposits of fat that can occur in the skin and are associated with high levels of cholesterol and triglycerides in the blood.",
