                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Can you explain what depressed mood means in this context?\n\nProfessor: Depressed mood refers to a persistent feeling of sadness, hopelessness, and loss of interest or pleasure in activities that the person normally enjoys.\n\nStudent: What are sleep disturbances?\n\nProfessor: Sleep disturbances refer to changes in the amount, quality, or timing of sleep. This can include difficulty falling asleep, staying asleep, or waking up too early.\n\nStudent: What is a poor appetite?\n\nProfessor: A poor appetite refers to a decrease in the desire to eat or a decrease in the amount of food that is consumed.\n\nStudent: Can you explain what elevated mood means?\n\nProfessor: Elevated mood refers to a persistent feeling of euphoria, grandiosity, or increased energy and activity levels.\n\nStudent: What is type I diabetes mellitus?\n\nProfessor: Type I diabetes mellitus is a chronic condition in which the pancreas produces little or no insulin, a hormone that regulates blood sugar levels. This requires the person to take insulin injections or use an insulin pump to manage their blood sugar levels.\n\nStudent: What is methotrexate?\n\nProfessor: Methotrexate is a medication that is commonly used to treat rheumatoid arthritis. It works by suppressing the immune system to reduce inflammation and pain.\n\nStudent: What is the difference between Bipolar I and Bipolar II disorder?\n\nProfessor: Bipolar I disorder is characterized by at least one manic episode, which is a period of abnormally elevated or irritable mood, along with increased energy and activity levels. Bipolar II disorder is characterized by at least one hypomanic episode, which is a less severe form of mania, along with at least one major depressive episode.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "a1869825-ab5e-49a9-bdc0-a17bbab1de3a",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-E",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "B) Bipolar II disorder.",
                                "correct_answer": false
                            }
                        ],
